  "prompt": "You are an associate analyst at Brennan Brothers & Co. in the Financial Institutions Group. Lin Wei-chen, your managing director, just assigned you a QoQ margin variance analysis for Goldman Sachs following their 424B2 filing today — this will feed directly into a client pitch deck discussion on GS's profitability trajectory.\n\n\n\nStart with Q1 2026 net income of $5.63B and derive total revenue from the consolidated statement of earnings in the Q1 2026 10-Q filing. The 424B2 is a prospectus supplement so you'll need to pull the full income statement detail and Q4 2025 comparative figures from EDGAR separately. Compute net profit margin for both quarters and quantify the absolute and percentage-point change QoQ. Then bridge the variance by itemizing key line-item drivers — think compensation & benefits expense, provision for credit losses, net interest income, and any meaningful revenue mix shifts across GS's three segments (Asset & Wealth Management, Global Banking & Markets, Platform Solutions) if segment data is available in the filing.\n\n\n\nAll dollar figures in millions with consistent rounding, and every data point should carry an EDGAR source citation. Structure the workbook with clearly labeled tabs — assumptions, calculations, and a summary layer. Include a brief interpretive write-up explaining the primary drivers of margin movement. Format it presentation-ready: blue header rows, clean number formats, no gridlines on the summary tabs. Lin will be pulling charts and tables directly from this, so the output needs to look like it belongs in a pitch book.\n\nI've attached GS_historical_financials.xlsx with five years of historical data that may be useful for context, but the core analysis should be built from the latest quarterly filings. Use GS's US GAAP consolidated statement of earnings structure — net interest income plus non-interest income — for revenue, and mark any items requiring analyst judgment with a clearly labeled assumption flag.",
